Setting the <tangent line> approximation equal to zero gives the <Newton root-finding iteration>
$$
\boxed{x_1=x_0-\frac{f(x_0)}{f'(x_0)}}.
$$
The step requires a nonzero <derivative> at the starting point.

= b
{parent=6}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Here $f(1)=-1$ and $f'(x)=1+1/x$, so $f'(1)=2$. The <Newton root-finding iteration> gives
$$
\boxed{x_1=1-\frac{-1}{2}=\frac32}.
$$

